"P 波反映心房的电活动，通常出现在 QRS 波群之前。这里看它持续多久、波峰有多高，以及波形朝上还是朝下。" = "The P wave reflects the atria's electrical activity and usually appears before the QRS complex. Here you can see its duration, peak height and whether it points up or down.";
"从 P 波开始到 QRS 波群开始，称为 PR 间期。这段时间帮助我们观察电信号从心房传到心室的过程。" = "The PR interval runs from the start of the P wave to the start of the QRS complex. It helps show how the electrical signal travels from the atria to the ventricles.";
"P 波结束后，到 QRS 波群开始前的短间隔。这里看它持续多久，以及波形相对参考水平线的位置。" = "This is the short segment between the end of the P wave and the start of the QRS complex. Here you can see its duration and its level relative to the reference baseline.";
"QRS 通常是心电图里较高、较尖的一组波形，反映心室的电活动。这里看整组持续多久，以及 Q、R、S 各部分的大小。" = "The QRS complex is usually the tall, sharp group of waves in an ECG. It reflects the ventricles' electrical activity. Here you can see its total duration and the size of the Q, R and S components.";
"ST 段位于 QRS 和 T 波之间，QRS 结束的位置叫 J 点。这里看波形相对参考水平线偏高还是偏低，以及变化的方向。" = "The ST segment lies between QRS and the T wave. The end of QRS is called the J point. Here you can see whether the waveform is above or below the reference baseline and which way it changes.";
"T 波反映心室电活动的恢复过程。这里看它持续多久、波峰大小，以及前后两部分的形状。" = "The T wave reflects electrical recovery of the ventricles. Here you can see its duration, peak size and the shape of its rising and falling parts.";
"从 QRS 开始到 T 波结束，称为 QT 间期。它包括心室电活动开始到恢复的整个过程。" = "The QT interval runs from the start of QRS to the end of the T wave. It covers the ventricles' electrical activity from activation through recovery.";
"心率快慢会影响 QT。QTc 根据心跳间隔作了换算，便于比较。下面列出两种常用算法，结果可能略有差别。" = "Heart rate affects QT. QTc adjusts QT using the heartbeat interval to make comparisons easier. Two common formulas are shown below; their results may differ slightly.";
"一次心跳的 T 波结束，到下一次 P 波开始的间隔。这段波形通常比较平缓，可用来确定测量时的参考水平线。" = "This segment runs from the end of one beat's T wave to the start of the next P wave. It is usually fairly flat and can provide a reference baseline for measurement.";
"RR 是相邻两个 R 波峰之间的时间，PP 则看相邻两个 P 波峰。它们分别反映心室和心房电活动的间隔。" = "RR is the time between consecutive R peaks; PP is the time between consecutive P peaks. They reflect the intervals between electrical activity in the ventricles and atria, respectively.";
"U 波有时出现在 T 波之后，通常很小，也容易与旁边的波形混在一起。目前应用还不能可靠地单独识别它。" = "A U wave sometimes appears after the T wave. It is usually small and easily blends into nearby waves. The app cannot yet identify it reliably on its own.";
"成人 P 波常用参考为短于 120 ms。波峰的大小还与记录的导联有关。" = "A common adult reference for P-wave duration is less than 120 ms. Peak height also depends on the recording lead.";
"成人常用参考为 120–200 ms。年龄、心率和测量方法都会影响结果。" = "A common adult reference is 120–200 ms. Age, heart rate and measurement method affect the result.";
"PR 段通常接近参考水平线。参考线的位置和信号处理方式会影响测量。" = "The PR segment is usually close to the reference baseline. Baseline placement and signal processing affect its measurement.";
"成人 QRS 常用参考为短于 120 ms。Q、R、S 的识别还需要结合原波形复核。" = "A common adult reference for QRS duration is less than 120 ms. Q, R and S identification should also be checked against the original trace.";
"接触、姿势和信号处理都可能改变 ST 的样子。手表心电不能据此判断或排除心肌缺血。" = "Contact, posture and signal processing can all change the ST segment's appearance. A Watch ECG cannot use this to diagnose or rule out myocardial ischemia.";
"从不同导联看，T 波的方向和大小可能不同，不能只凭一个数值判断是否正常。" = "T-wave direction and size vary by lead. A single value cannot determine whether it is normal.";
"QT 会随心率变化，不能用一个固定范围判断所有记录。" = "QT changes with heart rate, so one fixed range cannot be used to assess all records.";
"心率很快或很慢时，校正的偏差可能更大。解读还需结合年龄、性别和所用方法。" = "Correction can be less accurate at very fast or very slow heart rates. Interpretation also depends on age, sex and the formula used.";
"心跳较快时，这段间隔可能很短，甚至难以与相邻波形分开。" = "At faster heart rates, this segment may be very short or hard to separate from adjacent waves.";
"这些数字描述心跳间隔的变化，尚未区分正常心跳与其他类型，不能直接当作 HRV。" = "These values describe variation in heartbeat intervals. Normal beats have not been separated from other types, so they cannot be treated as HRV.";
"没有测量结果，不代表这条记录中没有 U 波。" = "No measurement does not mean there is no U wave in this record.";
"测量 P 波的开始、结束和峰值位置。波形太小、起止位置不清，或与旁边的波形重叠时，会留空相应数值。" = "The start, end and peak of the P wave are estimated. If it is too small, its boundaries are unclear or it overlaps nearby waves, the affected values are left blank.";
"使用同一次心跳的 P 波起点和 QRS 起点。任一位置不清楚时，不计算 PR 间期。PR 间期包括 P 波本身和后面的 PR 段。" = "Uses the P-wave start and QRS start from the same beat. If either is unclear, no PR interval is calculated. PR includes the P wave itself and the following PR segment.";
"从 P 波终点量到 QRS 起点；电位是这段波形相对局部 TP 参考线的平均值。正数表示在参考线上方，负数表示在下方。" = "Measured from the P-wave end to QRS start. The level is the mean voltage of this segment relative to the local TP baseline. Positive values are above the baseline; negative values are below it.";
"先估计 QRS 的开始和结束，再寻找主峰前后的反向波形，作为 Q、S 的候选。数值保留原来的正负方向；如果主峰朝下，Q、R、S 的命名需要人工复核。单导联无法判断电轴或胸前导联的 R 波变化。" = "QRS start and end are estimated first. Opposite-direction waves before and after the main peak are candidates for Q and S. Values retain their original polarity. If the main peak points down, Q, R and S labels need manual review. A single lead cannot assess the electrical axis or R-wave progression across chest leads.";
"以 QRS 终点估计 J 点，再测量其后 60 和 80 ms 的电位。变化速率由这两个位置的电位差计算；正值表示向上，负值表示向下。如果已接近 T 波，就不再把该处当作 ST 测量。" = "The QRS end estimates the J point. Voltage is measured 60 and 80 ms later. The change rate comes from the voltage difference between these positions: positive means upward and negative downward. Positions too close to the T wave are not used for ST measurements.";
"分别寻找 T 波的开始、峰值和结束。前后时长比 = 起点到峰值的时间 ÷ 峰值到终点的时间。两部分长度相近时，比值接近 1；有多个波峰时需要结合原图查看。" = "The T-wave start, peak and end are found separately. The duration ratio is start-to-peak time divided by peak-to-end time. It is near 1 when the two parts have similar lengths. Multiple peaks require checking the original trace.";
"每次心跳单独测量：从这一次 QRS 的起点，到同一次 T 波的终点，再汇总结果。T 波终点不清时，不计算 QT。" = "Each beat is measured separately, from its QRS start to its T-wave end, before results are summarized. If the T-wave end is unclear, QT is not calculated.";
"使用同一次心跳的 QT 和紧邻前一次的 RR，均以秒代入：Fridericia = QT / RR^(1/3)；Bazett = QT / √RR。当前算法要求相关 RR 连续、相邻变化不超过 10%，且间隔为 500–1500 ms。这是算法的适用条件，不是正常范围。" = "Uses QT from the same beat and the immediately preceding RR, both in seconds: Fridericia = QT / RR^(1/3); Bazett = QT / √RR. The algorithm requires continuous neighboring RR intervals, changes no greater than 10%, and intervals of 500–1500 ms. These are algorithm conditions, not a normal range.";
"从本次 T 波终点量到下一次 P 波起点。任一位置不清、信号中断，或间隔短于 40 ms 时不测量。" = "Measured from this T-wave end to the next P-wave start. No value is produced if either boundary is unclear, the signal has a gap, or the interval is shorter than 40 ms.";
"RR 和 PP 分别使用各自的相邻波峰计算，不互相替代，也不跨过信号中断的地方拼接。" = "RR and PP are calculated from their own consecutive peaks. They do not substitute for one another, and intervals are not joined across signal gaps.";
"目前无法可靠地把 U 波与 T 波末尾或下一次 P 波分开。可以打开单次心跳，查看原始波形。" = "The app cannot yet reliably separate U waves from the end of T or the next P wave. Open an individual beat to inspect the original trace.";
