"每个点连接前后两次心跳间隔；点越集中，间隔越相近。虚线椭圆表示一个标准差的分布，不是正常范围。" = "Each dot compares consecutive intervals. Tighter clusters mean more similar intervals. The dashed ellipse shows one standard deviation, not a normal range.";
"超短时 HRV 没有统一正常区间。呼吸、姿势、睡眠和压力都会影响数值，建议在相似条件下比较。" = "Ultra-short HRV has no universal normal range. Breathing, posture, sleep and stress affect it; compare under similar conditions.";
"SDNN 描述间隔的总体分散程度；RMSSD 描述相邻间隔的变化。SD1 和 SD2 分别表示聚集图横跨和沿着对角线的分散程度。" = "SDNN describes overall interval spread; RMSSD describes successive changes. SD1 and SD2 measure spread across and along the diagonal.";
"仅在来源为窦性心律且信号与节律满足条件时计算。排除被标记的心跳及其相邻间隔后，使用最长的连续片段，不跨空缺拼接或补值。" = "Calculated only for a sinus source classification with eligible signal and rhythm. Flagged beats and adjacent intervals are excluded; only the longest continuous run is used, without bridging or filling gaps.";
"筛选规则不能确认正常心跳，也可能漏检不规则节律；这些结果是研究性估算，不能用于诊断或与标准五分钟 HRV 等同。" = "Filtering cannot confirm normal beats and may miss irregular rhythms. These research estimates are not diagnostic or equivalent to standard five-minute HRV.";
"成人参考：P 波 < 120 ms" = "Adult reference: P wave < 120 ms";
"参考范围来自常规心电图；手表单导联的边界估算可能有偏差。" = "References come from conventional ECGs. Watch single-lead boundary estimates may differ.";
"成人参考：PR 120–200 ms" = "Adult reference: PR 120–200 ms";
"年龄、心率及药物会影响 PR，参考范围不能单独用于诊断。" = "Age, heart rate and medicines affect PR. The reference range alone cannot diagnose a condition.";
"成人参考：QRS < 120 ms" = "Adult reference: QRS < 120 ms";
"常见 QRS 约 70–100 ms；小于 120 ms 仅表示未达到常用增宽界限，不表示心电正常。" = "QRS is commonly about 70–100 ms. Below 120 ms only means below a common widening threshold, not a normal ECG.";
"成人 QTc：男性约 350–450 ms；女性约 360–460 ms" = "Adult QTc: men about 350–450 ms; women about 360–460 ms";
"成人静息参考：RR 600–1000 ms（60–100 bpm）" = "Adult resting reference: RR 600–1000 ms (60–100 bpm)";
"仅适用于成人安静状态。呼吸、运动、睡眠、体能和药物都可能改变心跳间隔。" = "For resting adults only. Breathing, exercise, sleep, fitness and medicines can alter intervals.";
"没有适用于本次单导联测量的统一正常区间" = "No universal normal range applies to this single-lead measurement";
